Security: Enforcement Runtime

Purpose:
  Runtime enforcement of .sdd security gates via claude-code hooks.
  Promotes advisory-only security checks (false-green gap) into
  enforced blocking at the tool-execution boundary.

  Integrates with:
    .sdd/security/levels.sdd (L0-L5 levels)
    .sdd/security/controls.sdd (pattern set, seeded from claude-code patterns.py)
    .sdd/gates/security.sdd (gate schema)
    .sdd/runtime/adapter-runtime.sdd (HookBridge)

EnforcementModel:
  observe:
    description: Advisory mode — warnings logged, tool proceeds
    triggers: PostToolUse[Edit/Write] pattern match at low L-level
    action: log OBS12 security_gate_warned, tool continues
    default_for: L0-L3 patterns below project threshold

  enforce:
    description: Blocking mode — tool call blocked on gate failure
    triggers: PostToolUse[Edit/Write] pattern match at HIGH/CRITICAL L-level
    action: emit OBS13 security_gate_blocked, exit 2 (block tool)
    default_for: L4-L5 patterns at or above project SecurityLevel threshold

ModeSelection:
  source: PROJECT.sdd SecurityLevel
  rule: L0-L2 -> observe (no blocking)
  rule: L3 -> observe with OBS12 for HIGH, enforce for CRITICAL
  rule: L4 -> enforce for HIGH and CRITICAL
  rule: L5 -> enforce for MEDIUM and above

PatternSet:
  source: claude-code plugins/security-guidance/hooks/patterns.py:30-345
  count: 17 pattern rules
  categories:
    - yaml.load (deserialization) -> L3 CRITICAL
    - pickle.loads/dumps (RCE) -> L4 CRITICAL
    - eval/exec (code injection) -> L4 CRITICAL
    - subprocess with shell=True (command injection) -> L3 HIGH
    - innerHTML/dangerouslySetInnerHTML (XSS) -> L2 HIGH
    - string SQL concatenation (SQL injection) -> L3 CRITICAL
    - hardcoded secrets (API key, token, password) -> L4 CRITICAL
    - random.random for tokens (weak crypto) -> L2 MEDIUM
    - MD5/SHA1 for security (weak crypto) -> L2 MEDIUM
    - unsanitized file paths (path traversal) -> L3 HIGH
    - CORS wildcard (CORS misconfiguration) -> L3 MEDIUM
    - missing auth check (broken access control) -> L4 CRITICAL
    - SSRF (server-side request forgery) -> L4 HIGH
    - open redirect -> L2 MEDIUM
    - deserialization of untrusted data -> L3 CRITICAL
    - regex denial of service (ReDoS) -> L1 LOW
    - missing rate limiting -> L1 LOW

GateExecution:
  flow:
    PostToolUse[Edit/Write] ->
      HookBridge reads .sdd/security/controls.sdd pattern set ->
      Regex match against edited file content ->
      If match: look up L-level + severity from pattern metadata ->
      Compare L-level to project SecurityLevel from PROJECT.sdd ->
      if pattern_L_level >= project_threshold:
        emit OBS13 security_gate_blocked ->
        exit 2 (block tool, surface error to agent) ->
      else:
        emit OBS12 security_gate_warned ->
        tool proceeds with warning

ObserveToEnforceMigration:
  phase_1: 2 weeks observe mode — emit OBS12 on all matches, no blocking
  phase_2: 1 week tune — adjust regex thresholds, add whitelist for false positives
  phase_3: activate enforce mode — exit 2 on HIGH/CRITICAL above threshold
  rollback: set PROJECT.sdd SecurityLevel back to L2 or below

FalsePositiveHandling:
  whitelist:
    source: .sdd/security/whitelist.sdd (project-specific)
    format: { pattern_id, file_glob, reason, expires, owner }
    rule: whitelisted pattern matches do NOT trigger gate
    rule: whitelist entries MUST have expiration date
    rule: expired entries auto-retire and emit OBS14

  human_override:
    trigger: gate blocked but false positive
    action: emit OBS15 security_gate_overridden
    rule: override MUST be logged with reason + approver
    rule: override does NOT change pattern set — only suppresses this instance

AuditTrail:
  every gate decision emits:
    OBS12: security_gate_warned (observe mode)
    OBS13: security_gate_blocked (enforce mode)
    OBS14: security_gate_whitelisted (whitelist match)
    OBS15: security_gate_overridden (human override)

  fields:
    timestamp, pattern_id, file, line, severity, L_level, project_level, mode, decision, evidence, hash

Rules:
  [SECV1] Security gate enforcement MUST read pattern set from .sdd/security/controls.sdd, not hard-coded.
  [SECV2] Pattern L-levels MUST come from .sdd/security/levels.sdd, not hard-coded.
  [SECV3] Project threshold MUST come from PROJECT.sdd SecurityLevel, not hard-coded.
  [SECV4] In observe mode, ALL matches MUST emit OBS12 (never silent).
  [SECV5] In enforce mode, HIGH/CRITICAL matches at or above threshold MUST exit non-zero.
  [SECV6] Whitelist MUST be project-scoped and time-bounded.
  [SECV7] Human override MUST NOT modify the pattern set — only suppress.
  [SECV8] Every gate decision MUST be auditable via OBS12-OBS15 events.
  [SECV9] Adapter MUST NOT block non-security tools — only Edit/Write hooks.
  [SECV10] Secrets in tool arguments MUST be scrubbed before logging.
  [SECV11] If claude-code hooks are unavailable, adapter MUST fail-open with OBS16 warning.
  [SECV12] Gate enforcement MUST support project-level disable (PROJECT.sdd opt-out).
  [SECV13] Gate MUST be diff-aware: only block on findings introduced by the change under review.
  [SECV14] Gate MUST use reachability classification: block on reachable+exploitable, warn on reachable+not-exploitable, log-only on unreachable.
  [SECV15] SemanticReview MUST validate findings against changed hunks only (diff-aware gating).
  [SECV16] SemanticReview MUST mark findings as verified/unverified based on supporting evidence.
  [SECV17] Exception workflows MUST be time-boxed (30-90 days) and auditable with named approver.
  [SECV18] Policy-as-code MUST be version-controlled and reviewed like code.

Navigation:
  Gates: @INDEX.sdd
  Security Levels: @levels.sdd
  Security Controls: @controls.sdd
  Adapter: @../runtime/adapter-runtime.sdd
  Observability: @../../observability/INDEX.sdd

State: +